      <h2>1. General Information</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy provides information on the processing of personal data when visiting the website “Bella Rybka — Psychology, Counselling, Authorship”, available at <a href="https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/</a> (hereinafter the “Website”), as well as when sending messages using the contact details provided on the Website.</p>
      <p>The personal data controller is Rybka Bella Shamilievna, a natural person carrying out activities in Georgia. The controller determines the purposes and means of personal data processing within the scope of her activities.</p>
      <p>Contact email address for enquiries concerning personal data processing: <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a>. Postal address for correspondence: 19 Pirosmani Street, Batumi 6010, Georgia.</p>
      <h2>2. Data Processing When Visiting the Website</h2>
      <p>The public pages are accessible without registration. The Website has no data collection forms, comments, reader accounts or integrated payments. The controller does not request a visitor’s name, telephone number, postal address or health information through the Website interface.</p>
      <p>When the Website is accessed, the delivery of web pages and the operation of the infrastructure may involve processing an IP address, request time, requested page address, technical information about the browser and device, HTTP request headers and information about information-security events. Depending on the circumstances, these data may constitute personal data.</p>
      <p>The purposes of processing are to provide access to the Website’s materials, ensure its functionality and security, diagnose technical faults and prevent misuse. Where applicable, processing is based on the controller’s legitimate interest in operating and protecting the Website, subject to the requirements of applicable law and the rights of data subjects.</p>
      <h2>3. Use of Cloudflare Infrastructure</h2>
      <p>Cloudflare Pages is used to host and deliver the Website’s pages. When processing requests, Cloudflare may receive technical connection data and apply network protection mechanisms. The specific categories of data and their retention periods depend on the functions actually used and Cloudflare’s terms of service.</p>
      <p>Because Cloudflare uses international infrastructure, technical data may be processed outside Georgia. Applicable requirements governing cross-border transfers of data are taken into account in accordance with Georgian law. Further information: <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/</a>.</p>
      <h2>4. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p>The controller has not implemented web analytics tools, advertising pixels, marketing cookies or visitor behavioural profiling systems on the Website.</p>
      <p>When certain Cloudflare security functions are used, technical cookies, including __cf_bm or cf_clearance, may be set. Their actual presence depends on the security settings and the circumstances of a particular visit to the Website. These cookies are intended to support the relevant protective mechanisms, not for advertising tracking by the controller.</p>
      <p>Information on Cloudflare cookies: <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/</a>. If technologies requiring prior consent are introduced on the Website, information about them and the necessary consent mechanism will be provided before they are enabled.</p>
      <h2>5. External Resources and Enquiries</h2>
      <p>The Website contains ordinary links to Telegram, Instagram and Gmail’s email-composition service. Following a link takes the visitor to an external resource; the subsequent processing of data by the relevant provider is governed by its terms and privacy documentation.</p>
      <p>When a person voluntarily contacts the controller by email at <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a> or through the listed social networks, the controller receives information contained in the message, such as an email address or profile identifier, name or pseudonym, message text and voluntarily attached materials. These data are used to consider the enquiry and respond to it or, where the enquiry concerns cooperation, to discuss potential collaboration.</p>
      <p>No separate visitor database or register of enquiries is maintained. However, messages may be retained in the email inbox or the relevant messaging service. It is not recommended to send sensitive information through open communication channels unless necessary for the enquiry.</p>
      <h2>6. Retention Periods and Protective Measures</h2>
      <p>Technical data are processed to the extent and for the periods determined by the purposes of the services used, their settings and applicable legal requirements. The controller does not state a single retention period for records generated by Cloudflare.</p>
      <p>Correspondence is retained for as long as necessary to respond, continue communication, protect legitimate interests or fulfil legal obligations. When the legal basis and need for retention cease, messages accessible to the controller are to be deleted; data and backup copies held by service providers may remain under their rules and within applicable legal limits.</p>
      <p>HTTPS is used to transmit the Website’s pages. Access to Website management tools and correspondence is restricted; proportionate measures are applied to protect accounts and information.</p>
      <h2>7. Rights of Data Subjects</h2>
      <p>Under applicable law, a data subject may request information about processing and access to their data, seek rectification, completion, blocking, erasure or cessation of processing, and exercise other rights provided by law. Where processing is based on consent, that consent may be withdrawn within the limits established by law.</p>
      <p>Requests should be sent to <a href="mailto:x88tsar@gmail.com">x88tsar@gmail.com</a>. Where necessary, the controller may request proportionate information to verify the applicant’s identity or authority. Enquiries are considered within the time limits prescribed by applicable law.</p>
      <p>In the event of an alleged infringement of rights, a data subject may apply to the State Audit Office of Georgia or a court in accordance with the procedure established by law.</p>
      <h2>8. Amendments to the Policy</h2>
      <p>The Policy is reviewed when the purposes or methods of processing, the services used or the contact details change. The current version, showing its date of amendment, is published at <a href="https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://bella-shamilevna.pages.dev/privacy-policy/</a>.</p>
